1
00:03:03,950 --> 00:03:05,460
Easy, easy.

2
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:06,920
Easy.

3
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:16,240
What do you remember?

4
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:24,850
They stabbed me.

5
00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:30,750
Olly...

6
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:35,560
he put a knife in my heart.

7
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:43,480
I shouldn't be here.

8
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:47,370
The lady brought you back.

9
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:51,960
Afterwards, after they stabbed you,

10
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:54,210
after you died, where did you go?

11
00:03:54,530 --> 00:03:55,710
What did you see?

12
00:04:01,130 --> 00:04:02,090
Nothing.

13
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:07,120
There was nothing at all.

14
00:04:11,990 --> 00:04:14,140
The Lord let you come back for a reason.

15
00:04:16,970 --> 00:04:19,050
Stannis was not the prince who was promised,

16
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:20,850
but someone has to be.

17
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:27,190
Could you give us a moment?

18
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:49,390
You were dead.

19
00:04:50,530 --> 00:04:51,610
And now you're not.

20
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:57,410
That's completely fucking mad, seems to me.

21
00:04:58,050 --> 00:05:00,150
I can only imagine how it seems to you.

22
00:05:02,750 --> 00:05:04,550
I did what I thought was right.

23
00:05:07,580 --> 00:05:09,280
And I got murdered for it.

24
00:05:09,910 --> 00:05:11,150
And now I'm back.

25
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:13,430
Why?

26
00:05:13,830 --> 00:05:14,850
I don't know.

27
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:16,890
Maybe we'll never know.

28
00:05:18,050 --> 00:05:19,320
What does it matter?

29
00:05:22,490 --> 00:05:23,510
You go on.

30
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:27,910
You fight for as long as you can.

31
00:05:28,530 --> 00:05:30,980
You clean up as much of the shit as you can.

32
00:05:32,370 --> 00:05:33,940
I don't know how to do that.

33
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:37,810
I thought I did, but...

34
00:05:42,290 --> 00:05:43,480
I failed.

35
00:05:46,670 --> 00:05:47,590
Good.

36
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,590
Now go fail again.

37
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:49,220
They think you're some kind of god.

38
00:06:49,850 --> 00:06:52,390
The man who returned from the dead.

39
00:06:52,390 --> 00:06:53,540
I'm not a god.

40
00:06:54,930 --> 00:06:56,000
I know that.

41
00:06:58,260 --> 00:06:59,760
I saw your pecker.

42
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:03,240
What kind of god would have a pecker that small?

43
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:30,180
Your eyes are still brown.

44
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:33,510
Is that still you in there?

45
00:07:34,070 --> 00:07:35,180
I think so.

46
00:07:38,410 --> 00:07:40,380
Hold off on burning my body for now.

47
00:07:43,270 --> 00:07:44,290
That's funny.

48
00:07:47,310 --> 00:07:48,960
You sure that's still you in there?

49
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:21,840
You all right?

50
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:25,050
Yes. Yes, I'm fine.

51
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:32,040
Did I ever tell you I used to think the sea was called the see

52
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:34,980
because it was nothing but water as far as the eye could see?

53
00:08:35,350 --> 00:08:36,560
I don't think so.

54
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:38,640
Sea, see.

55
00:08:39,220 --> 00:08:41,800
They're spelled different, but they sound the same.

56
00:08:43,110 --> 00:08:44,980
Yeah, they do.

57
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:47,680
It was before I learned how to read, obviously.

58
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:54,000
Sam, are you going to be sick?

59
00:09:09,150 --> 00:09:11,970
Won't be long. We'll be in the south soon.

60
00:09:12,130 --> 00:09:14,170
I'm excited to see Oldtown.

61
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:19,300
Captain says it's the most beautiful city in Westeros.

62
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:22,780
Are you going to vomit again?

63
00:09:22,790 --> 00:09:24,940
No. No, no, no.

64
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:29,420
The Citadel doesn't admit women.

65
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:32,580
There won't be a place for you there or for Little Sam.

66
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:36,280
I stayed at Castle Black. There's no women allowed there.

67
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:38,450
The Citadel isn't Castle Black.

68
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:43,280
I don't have a Jon Snow or Maester Aemon to help me bend the rules.

69
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:46,790
I'll stay in Oldtown, then.

70
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:48,000
By yourself?

71
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:50,120
With a baby and no money?

72
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:55,000
So if we're not going to Oldtown, where are you taking me?

73
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,310
To my home.

74
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,230
Horn Hill.

75
00:10:01,980 --> 00:10:04,760
My father's-- well, my father,

76
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:07,780
but my mother's a kind woman and my sister's lovely.

77
00:10:08,570 --> 00:10:10,800
They'll take care of you both.

78
00:10:12,290 --> 00:10:14,510
"Wherever you go, I go, too."

79
00:10:14,510 --> 00:10:15,960
That's what you said.

80
00:10:32,850 --> 00:10:35,950
I said that because I want you and Little Sam to be safe.

81
00:10:36,650 --> 00:10:38,000
That's all I want--

82
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:41,760
to become a maester so I can help Jon when the time comes

83
00:10:42,210 --> 00:10:43,740
so you'll be safe.

84
00:10:43,930 --> 00:10:45,530
Us and everyone else in the world.

85
00:10:45,540 --> 00:10:47,450
I don't care about them.

86
00:10:47,770 --> 00:10:51,590
Well, no, I do, but I don't really.

87
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:55,160
I care about you and him.

88
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:59,140
I know that, Sam.

89
00:10:59,750 --> 00:11:01,300
And he does, too.

90
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:07,130
You're the only one who ever has.

91
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:17,830
If you think it's for the best,

92
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:19,550
we trust you.

93
00:11:21,170 --> 00:11:24,370
I'd feel better if you threw something at me and stormed off.

94
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:27,760
I'd never do that to the father of my son.

95
00:12:25,250 --> 00:12:26,440
That's my father.

96
00:12:28,290 --> 00:12:31,720
The man beside him is Howland Reed, meera's father.

97
00:12:43,980 --> 00:12:45,120
Ser Arthur Dayne.

98
00:12:45,830 --> 00:12:47,390
The Sword of the Morning.

99
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:50,850
Father said he was the best swordsman he ever saw.

100
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,500
Lord Stark.

101
00:13:07,530 --> 00:13:09,190
I looked for you on the Trident.

102
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,320
We weren't there.

103
00:13:12,430 --> 00:13:13,760
Your friend the usurper

104
00:13:13,770 --> 00:13:15,890
would lie beneath the ground if we had been.

105
00:13:17,170 --> 00:13:18,640
The Mad King is dead.

106
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:21,260
Rhaegar lies beneath the ground.

107
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:23,850
Why weren't you there to protect your prince?

108
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:25,590
Our prince wanted us here.

109
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:34,840
Where's my sister?

110
00:13:37,830 --> 00:13:40,070
I wish you good fortune in the wars to come.

111
00:13:47,730 --> 00:13:48,950
And now it begins.

112
00:13:54,740 --> 00:13:55,690
No.

113
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,220
Now it ends.

114
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:37,160
He's better than my father.

115
00:15:38,110 --> 00:15:39,260
Far better.

116
00:15:44,670 --> 00:15:45,870
But Father beat him.

117
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:48,260
Did he?

118
00:15:49,510 --> 00:15:50,640
I know he did.

119
00:15:50,910 --> 00:15:52,650
Heard the story a thousand times.

120
00:16:10,550 --> 00:16:12,050
He stabbed him in the back.

121
00:16:31,610 --> 00:16:32,840
What's in the tower?

122
00:16:33,390 --> 00:16:34,920
That's enough for one day.

123
00:16:35,420 --> 00:16:36,840
We'll visit again another time.

124
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:39,250
- I want to see where he's going. - Time to go.

125
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:42,070
Father!

126
00:17:08,980 --> 00:17:10,320
Why did you do that?

127
00:17:10,430 --> 00:17:12,440
Take me back there. I want to go back.

128
00:17:12,890 --> 00:17:13,970
No.

129
00:17:16,020 --> 00:17:18,260
- He heard me. - Maybe.

130
00:17:18,610 --> 00:17:21,190
- Maybe he heard the wind. - He heard me.

131
00:17:21,670 --> 00:17:25,180
The past is already written. The ink is dry.

132
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:26,950
What's in that tower?

133
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:28,800
I want to go back there.

134
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:32,430
I've told you many times, stay too long where you don't belong

135
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:34,200
and you will never return.

136
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:35,800
Why do I want to return?

137
00:17:36,220 --> 00:17:38,050
So I can be a cripple again?

138
00:17:38,090 --> 00:17:40,330
So I can talk to an old man in a tree?

139
00:17:40,330 --> 00:17:42,520
You think I wanted to sit here for 1,000 years

140
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:44,550
watching the world from a distance

141
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:46,140
as the roots grew through me?

142
00:17:46,140 --> 00:17:47,550
So why did you?

143
00:17:49,090 --> 00:17:50,810
I was waiting for you.

144
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:52,780
I don't want to be you.

145
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:55,240
I don't blame you.

146
00:17:56,650 --> 00:17:58,690
You won't be here forever.

147
00:17:59,070 --> 00:18:01,910
You won't be an old man in a tree.

148
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:04,120
But before you leave,

149
00:18:04,310 --> 00:18:07,060
you must learn.

150
00:18:07,810 --> 00:18:09,070
Learn what?

151
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:11,460
Everything.

152
00:22:05,510 --> 00:22:08,250
I don't know how you stand it in all that leather.

153
00:22:15,910 --> 00:22:17,270
If we could have the room.

154
00:22:28,060 --> 00:22:30,360
You look lovely today, my dear. You really do.

155
00:22:30,910 --> 00:22:34,740
How you climbed all those steps without breaking a sweat.

156
00:22:34,910 --> 00:22:36,240
If you're going to torture me,

157
00:22:36,240 --> 00:22:38,300
just call them back and get on with it.

158
00:22:38,530 --> 00:22:40,210
I am not a torturer.

159
00:22:42,050 --> 00:22:45,430
Though it so often is what people deserve.

160
00:22:46,650 --> 00:22:49,110
And it does provide answers.

161
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:52,470
But they're usually the wrong answers.

162
00:22:52,900 --> 00:22:56,100
My job is to find the right answers.

163
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:57,910
Do you know how I do that?

164
00:22:58,560 --> 00:23:01,140
I do it by making people happy.

165
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:04,500
I'd like to make you happy, Vala.

166
00:23:04,830 --> 00:23:07,410
That's your name, isn't it, Vala?

167
00:23:08,770 --> 00:23:10,020
That's all right.

168
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:13,380
I know who you are and what you've done.

169
00:23:14,910 --> 00:23:16,120
You've done a lot.

170
00:23:16,650 --> 00:23:19,040
You've sacrificed your body for a cause,

171
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:20,990
which is more than most people do.

172
00:23:23,290 --> 00:23:27,250
And you've helped the Sons of the Harpy murder the Unsullied

173
00:23:27,250 --> 00:23:28,550
and the Second Sons.

174
00:23:28,550 --> 00:23:32,400
The Unsullied and the Second Sons are foreign soldiers

175
00:23:32,500 --> 00:23:34,020
brought here by a foreign queen

176
00:23:34,020 --> 00:23:36,380
to destroy our city and our history.

177
00:23:37,910 --> 00:23:39,170
I understand.

178
00:23:40,450 --> 00:23:42,260
Well, that makes perfect sense

179
00:23:42,670 --> 00:23:44,420
from your perspective.

180
00:23:45,730 --> 00:23:49,180
I have a different perspective, of course.

181
00:23:49,780 --> 00:23:50,650
I think it's important

182
00:23:50,650 --> 00:23:52,830
that you try to see things from my perspective

183
00:23:52,830 --> 00:23:55,240
just as I will try to see them from yours.

184
00:23:55,890 --> 00:23:57,620
Because that is the only way

185
00:23:57,630 --> 00:24:00,650
that I can make you and Dom happy.

186
00:24:03,690 --> 00:24:06,720
That is how you pronounce it-- Dom?

187
00:24:07,860 --> 00:24:10,620
I'm afraid I don't really speak the language.

188
00:24:12,090 --> 00:24:13,910
Such a handsome boy.

189
00:24:14,100 --> 00:24:17,620
Those big, brown eyes. Good luck keeping the ladies away.

190
00:24:18,860 --> 00:24:21,900
Yes, you're a true liberator, aren't you?

191
00:24:22,340 --> 00:24:25,230
You won't torture me, you'll just threaten my son.

192
00:24:25,860 --> 00:24:27,430
Children are blameless.

193
00:24:28,450 --> 00:24:30,320
I have never hurt them.

194
00:24:31,140 --> 00:24:32,870
Your boy is in no immediate danger,

195
00:24:32,870 --> 00:24:34,910
this I swear to you.

196
00:24:36,840 --> 00:24:38,400
But between us, dear,

197
00:24:39,080 --> 00:24:41,860
you did conspire to kill the Queen's soldiers.

198
00:24:41,860 --> 00:24:44,590
We both know the penalty for that crime.

199
00:24:50,040 --> 00:24:52,830
How will poor Dom get on without his mother?

200
00:24:53,540 --> 00:24:55,450
And with his breathing problem.

201
00:24:55,450 --> 00:24:57,450
If I tell you anything, they'll kill me.

202
00:24:58,310 --> 00:25:00,330
So either you kill me or they do.

203
00:25:00,330 --> 00:25:03,660
Yes, from your perspective, this is a problem.

204
00:25:05,390 --> 00:25:07,300
There is a third option, though.

205
00:25:07,590 --> 00:25:10,780
A ship leaving tomorrow for Pentos.

206
00:25:10,780 --> 00:25:14,850
I've already booked passage for a woman and her young son.

207
00:25:15,850 --> 00:25:19,140
I'll even throw in a bag of silver to help you start again.

208
00:25:19,140 --> 00:25:20,950
Though I'm afraid we'll have to ask

209
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:24,420
one of our leather-clad friends back in to carry it.

210
00:25:24,550 --> 00:25:26,460
Far too heavy for me.

211
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:29,620
The boat sails at dawn.

212
00:25:30,110 --> 00:25:32,090
You need to decide now.

213
00:25:33,010 --> 00:25:35,370
A new life for you and Dom

214
00:25:35,790 --> 00:25:36,930
or...

215
00:25:53,250 --> 00:25:54,900
What should we do while we wait?

216
00:25:55,110 --> 00:25:56,870
To pass the time, what should we do?

217
00:25:57,220 --> 00:25:58,680
What should we talk about?

218
00:26:01,970 --> 00:26:03,680
You speak 19 languages.

219
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:06,470
You must occasionally use some of them to talk about things.

220
00:26:07,300 --> 00:26:10,350
You two, you spend a great deal of time together.

221
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:13,110
What would you be talking about if I weren't here?

222
00:26:14,310 --> 00:26:15,610
Patrol.

223
00:26:16,930 --> 00:26:19,670
When I am going on patrol with the Unsullied.

224
00:26:20,170 --> 00:26:21,910
What we see on patrol.

225
00:26:22,510 --> 00:26:24,180
Who we captured on patrol.

226
00:26:24,420 --> 00:26:26,460
That's good. That's very good.

227
00:26:28,730 --> 00:26:30,400
But that's a report.

228
00:26:31,420 --> 00:26:33,470
I was thinking more of a conversation.

229
00:26:33,930 --> 00:26:36,550
A wise man once said the true history of the world

230
00:26:36,550 --> 00:26:40,380
is the history of great conversations in elegant rooms.

231
00:26:41,160 --> 00:26:42,470
Who said this?

232
00:26:43,320 --> 00:26:44,440
Me.

233
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:46,140
Just now.

234
00:26:53,030 --> 00:26:54,840
All right, no conversations.

235
00:26:55,380 --> 00:26:56,890
Let's play a game.

236
00:26:59,770 --> 00:27:01,910
You don't play games, either one of you, ever?

237
00:27:01,910 --> 00:27:03,110
Games are for children.

238
00:27:03,110 --> 00:27:06,650
My master Kraznys would sometimes make us play games.

239
00:27:06,650 --> 00:27:08,880
There, that's a start.

240
00:27:09,230 --> 00:27:12,400
- Only the girls. - No, no, no.

241
00:27:12,960 --> 00:27:14,530
Not that. Of course not that.

242
00:27:16,150 --> 00:27:18,230
Innocent games. Fun games.

243
00:27:18,230 --> 00:27:19,660
Drinking games.

244
00:27:20,080 --> 00:27:21,700
We do not drink.

245
00:27:22,370 --> 00:27:23,990
Until you do.

246
00:27:26,480 --> 00:27:28,210
All right. No drinking.

247
00:27:28,210 --> 00:27:29,610
We can play without drinking.

248
00:27:30,160 --> 00:27:32,190
It's a wonderful game. I invented it.

249
00:27:32,190 --> 00:27:33,390
Here's how it works.

250
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:35,820
I make a statement about your past.

251
00:27:35,820 --> 00:27:37,720
If I'm wrong, I drink.

252
00:27:37,970 --> 00:27:39,280
And if I'm right--

253
00:27:41,390 --> 00:27:43,290
maybe we can't play without drinking.

254
00:27:46,100 --> 00:27:48,550
Oh, you took your time.

255
00:27:49,360 --> 00:27:50,590
Sorry.

256
00:27:50,680 --> 00:27:54,400
I was busy learning who funds the Sons of the Harpy.

257
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:56,620
- Some things you can't rush. - You found out?

258
00:27:56,620 --> 00:27:58,840
The Good Masters of Astapor

259
00:27:58,840 --> 00:28:01,330
and the Wise Masters of Yunkai.

260
00:28:01,440 --> 00:28:04,290
With help from their friends in Volantis.

261
00:28:04,290 --> 00:28:05,570
You see?

262
00:28:05,820 --> 00:28:08,120
You don't even have to worry about the local rebellion.

263
00:28:08,510 --> 00:28:09,840
We only have to worry about

264
00:28:09,840 --> 00:28:12,260
the three rich foreign cities paying for it.

265
00:28:12,260 --> 00:28:14,010
We conquered Astapor and Yunkai once.

266
00:28:14,010 --> 00:28:16,220
We will do it again and execute the Masters.

267
00:28:16,220 --> 00:28:19,170
If the Unsullied march off to reconquer Astapor and Yunkai,

268
00:28:19,180 --> 00:28:21,120
who will remain to defend the free people of Meereen?

269
00:28:21,120 --> 00:28:23,400
If we do not fight them, how can we stop them?

270
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:24,810
We cannot.

271
00:28:25,330 --> 00:28:28,220
The Masters speak only one language.

272
00:28:28,480 --> 00:28:30,170
They spoke it to me for many years.

273
00:28:30,170 --> 00:28:32,020
I know it better than my mother tongue.

274
00:28:32,050 --> 00:28:35,440
If we want them to hear us, we must speak it back to them.

275
00:28:35,950 --> 00:28:38,150
May it be the last thing they ever hear.

276
00:28:39,050 --> 00:28:40,250
You may be right.

277
00:28:40,250 --> 00:28:41,690
So we will fight them?

278
00:28:42,210 --> 00:28:44,250
- Possibly. - Possibly?

279
00:28:44,850 --> 00:28:46,490
It's a conversation.

280
00:28:47,420 --> 00:28:49,700
Tell me, can your little birds get a message

281
00:28:49,700 --> 00:28:52,890
to the Good Masters of Astapor, the Wise Masters of Yunkai,

282
00:28:52,890 --> 00:28:55,440
and benevolent enslavers of Volantis?

283
00:28:55,650 --> 00:28:58,170
Of course. Men can be fickle,

284
00:28:58,170 --> 00:29:00,670
but birds I always trust.

285
00:29:08,060 --> 00:29:10,110
Your eye looks much better, Arthur.

286
00:29:10,730 --> 00:29:12,380
How's your mother's jaw?

287
00:29:12,390 --> 00:29:13,590
Better.

288
00:29:14,190 --> 00:29:15,550
And your father?

289
00:29:16,250 --> 00:29:17,840
No one's seen him.

290
00:29:17,840 --> 00:29:19,260
And no one will.

291
00:29:19,280 --> 00:29:20,930
That worked out rather nicely.

292
00:29:20,930 --> 00:29:23,210
Will Lord Varys ever come back?

293
00:29:23,300 --> 00:29:24,810
I don't think so.

294
00:29:25,540 --> 00:29:26,820
Do you miss him?

295
00:29:27,470 --> 00:29:28,840
He was nice.

296
00:29:30,170 --> 00:29:32,320
He called us his little birds.

297
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:34,150
He gave us sweets.

298
00:29:36,220 --> 00:29:38,420
It's funny you should mention that.

299
00:29:40,340 --> 00:29:44,140
Guess what I happened to find today.

300
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:47,730
Candied plums from Dorne.

301
00:29:51,940 --> 00:29:54,080
Now remember, if any of your friends

302
00:29:54,090 --> 00:29:57,350
like sweets or need help, they can always come to me.

303
00:29:57,350 --> 00:30:02,000
All I need in return are whispers.

304
00:30:09,350 --> 00:30:11,220
No need to be afraid.

305
00:30:11,650 --> 00:30:13,170
This is Ser Gregor.

306
00:30:13,370 --> 00:30:15,700
He's friends with all my friends.

307
00:30:20,950 --> 00:30:22,330
Run along now.

308
00:30:27,830 --> 00:30:29,500
Varys's little birds?

309
00:30:29,560 --> 00:30:31,330
Your little birds now, Your Grace.

310
00:30:31,330 --> 00:30:33,290
What did you do to him exactly?

311
00:30:33,300 --> 00:30:35,170
I haven't been able to get a clear answer.

312
00:30:35,170 --> 00:30:37,250
Oh, a number of things.

313
00:30:37,250 --> 00:30:38,690
Does he understand what we're saying?

314
00:30:38,690 --> 00:30:41,170
I mean, to the extent that he ever understood

315
00:30:41,170 --> 00:30:43,650
complete sentences in the first place.

316
00:30:45,200 --> 00:30:47,300
He understands well enough.

317
00:30:47,300 --> 00:30:49,490
So tell him to march into the sept

318
00:30:49,500 --> 00:30:52,220
and crush the High Sparrow's head like a melon.

319
00:30:52,220 --> 00:30:55,820
The High Sparrow has hundreds of Faith Militant surrounding him.

320
00:30:55,820 --> 00:30:57,990
Ser Gregor can't face them all.

321
00:30:58,170 --> 00:30:59,750
And he won't have to.

322
00:31:00,240 --> 00:31:02,070
He'll only have to face one.

323
00:31:04,650 --> 00:31:06,800
Has the Faith leveled official charges yet?

324
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:08,080
Not yet.

325
00:31:08,460 --> 00:31:11,830
That is one trial by combat I look forward to watching.

326
00:31:11,830 --> 00:31:13,480
Don't stop at the city.

327
00:31:14,030 --> 00:31:16,140
I want little birds in Dorne,

328
00:31:16,320 --> 00:31:19,090
in Highgarden, in the North.

329
00:31:19,120 --> 00:31:22,080
If someone is planning on making our losses their gains,

330
00:31:22,080 --> 00:31:23,760
I want to hear it.

331
00:31:24,760 --> 00:31:26,720
If someone is laughing at the queen

332
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:29,460
who walked naked through the streets covered in shit,

333
00:31:29,460 --> 00:31:31,050
I want to hear.

334
00:31:31,740 --> 00:31:33,760
I want to know who they are.

335
00:31:34,470 --> 00:31:36,240
I want to know where they are.

336
00:31:42,850 --> 00:31:45,800
As bad as Lord Varys was, Qyburn is worse.

337
00:31:45,810 --> 00:31:48,040
I told them all. I told them.

338
00:31:48,040 --> 00:31:50,460
He's arrogant, dangerous.

339
00:31:50,460 --> 00:31:53,460
You don't get thrown out of the Citadel without good reason.

340
00:31:53,460 --> 00:31:55,270
And no one listened to my advice.

341
00:31:55,270 --> 00:31:56,980
So here we are.

342
00:31:57,180 --> 00:31:59,600
And what he's done to Gregor Clegane

343
00:31:59,600 --> 00:32:01,270
is an abomination.

344
00:32:01,770 --> 00:32:04,780
We never sanctioned this experiment.

345
00:32:05,130 --> 00:32:07,480
I for one think it will be in our best interest

346
00:32:07,480 --> 00:32:09,170
to have the beast dest--

347
00:32:14,800 --> 00:32:16,770
- Can I help you? - Why are you here?

348
00:32:16,780 --> 00:32:19,310
- My mother-- - I was invited, my dear,

349
00:32:19,310 --> 00:32:22,260
to help deal with several troublesome issues,

350
00:32:22,290 --> 00:32:24,600
such as the queen's imprisonment.

351
00:32:24,610 --> 00:32:26,520
Thank you for bringing it up.

352
00:32:27,010 --> 00:32:30,990
It's well past time we addressed the abuses I endured.

353
00:32:31,040 --> 00:32:33,010
Margaery is the queen.

354
00:32:33,020 --> 00:32:35,100
You are not the queen

355
00:32:35,100 --> 00:32:37,090
because you're not married to the king.

356
00:32:37,090 --> 00:32:38,860
I do appreciate these things

357
00:32:38,860 --> 00:32:42,080
can get a bit confusing in your family.

358
00:32:42,910 --> 00:32:44,850
This is a small council meeting.

359
00:32:44,850 --> 00:32:47,220
You have no position on the small council.

360
00:32:47,220 --> 00:32:49,010
I'm the Lord Commander of the Kingsguard.

361
00:32:49,010 --> 00:32:50,640
The Lord Commander of the Kingsguard

362
00:32:50,650 --> 00:32:52,490
does have a position on the small council.

363
00:32:52,490 --> 00:32:55,560
Grand Maester Pycelle, would you sanction that statement?

364
00:32:55,690 --> 00:32:57,020
Well, um...

365
00:32:57,020 --> 00:33:00,190
I would say Ser Gerold Hightower

366
00:33:00,190 --> 00:33:02,590
had a seat on the Mad King's council.

367
00:33:02,670 --> 00:33:04,990
Of course, that was the Mad King.

368
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:06,890
King Robert saw things differently.

369
00:33:06,890 --> 00:33:08,180
And King-- -

370
00:33:11,740 --> 00:33:14,020
What about Myrcella's death, Uncle?

371
00:33:14,850 --> 00:33:16,960
Do you consider the murder of your own blood

372
00:33:16,960 --> 00:33:18,850
a troublesome issue?

373
00:33:19,280 --> 00:33:21,140
The same women who murdered Myrcella

374
00:33:21,140 --> 00:33:23,800
have overthrown House Martell and taken control of Dorne.

375
00:33:23,800 --> 00:33:25,340
We've got a lot to discuss.

376
00:33:25,340 --> 00:33:26,950
All of us together.

377
00:33:28,660 --> 00:33:30,400
And seeing as you cannot make us leave,

378
00:33:30,400 --> 00:33:31,730
we best get on with it.

379
00:33:33,600 --> 00:33:35,410
No, we cannot make you leave.

380
00:33:36,290 --> 00:33:38,680
And you cannot make us stay.

381
00:33:39,790 --> 00:33:43,250
Not unless you're gonna have that thing murder us all.

382
00:34:25,520 --> 00:34:26,640
Your Grace.

383
00:34:26,640 --> 00:34:29,940
My mother would like to see her daughter's final resting place.

384
00:34:30,240 --> 00:34:32,290
I'm sorry, Your Grace.

385
00:34:32,500 --> 00:34:34,560
That's not possible. Not yet.

386
00:34:34,560 --> 00:34:36,350
When will it be possible?

387
00:34:36,350 --> 00:34:38,600
When she's fully atoned for her sins.

388
00:34:38,600 --> 00:34:41,230
You cut off her hair and marched her naked

389
00:34:41,230 --> 00:34:43,620
through the streets in front of the whole city.

390
00:34:43,620 --> 00:34:45,620
That wasn't the full atonement?

391
00:34:45,780 --> 00:34:46,930
No.

392
00:34:47,480 --> 00:34:50,400
She must stand trial before seven septons

393
00:34:50,690 --> 00:34:53,040
so we can learn the true extent of her sins.

394
00:34:53,040 --> 00:34:56,970
I want you to let her see Myrcella's resting place.

395
00:34:56,970 --> 00:34:58,770
I am the king.

396
00:34:58,770 --> 00:35:00,090
You are.

397
00:35:02,570 --> 00:35:04,370
And what does that mean to you?

398
00:35:04,370 --> 00:35:05,970
It means a great deal to me.

399
00:35:05,970 --> 00:35:07,880
The Crown and the Faith

400
00:35:07,880 --> 00:35:10,180
are the twin pillars of the world.

401
00:35:10,490 --> 00:35:12,250
Do you know who told me that?

402
00:35:14,030 --> 00:35:15,220
Your mother.

403
00:35:15,220 --> 00:35:17,090
My mother who is unclean?

404
00:35:17,590 --> 00:35:19,010
My mother who still needs

405
00:35:19,010 --> 00:35:21,560
to atone after all you've put her through?

406
00:35:40,540 --> 00:35:43,640
How do you think the Mother Above first came to us?

407
00:35:44,370 --> 00:35:46,460
How did men and women

408
00:35:46,460 --> 00:35:49,940
first come to feel the Mother's presence, hmm?

409
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:53,150
It was through their own mothers.

410
00:35:55,900 --> 00:35:59,330
There's a great deal of falsehood in Cersei. You know that.

411
00:35:59,330 --> 00:36:03,530
But when she speaks of you, the Mother's love outshines it all.

412
00:36:05,480 --> 00:36:08,450
Her love for you is more real

413
00:36:08,450 --> 00:36:10,150
than anything else in this world

414
00:36:10,380 --> 00:36:12,860
because it doesn't come from this world.

415
00:36:13,900 --> 00:36:15,780
But you know that.

416
00:36:16,170 --> 00:36:17,630
You've felt it.

417
00:36:18,500 --> 00:36:20,480
You've seen her when she talks to you.

418
00:36:22,970 --> 00:36:24,120
Yes.

419
00:36:24,530 --> 00:36:26,200
It's a great gift.

420
00:36:26,480 --> 00:36:28,290
One I never had.

421
00:36:30,440 --> 00:36:31,720
Envy.

422
00:36:32,650 --> 00:36:35,120
One more thing for me to atone for.

423
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:38,330
Your Grace, do you-- may I?

424
00:36:38,340 --> 00:36:39,200
Do you mind?

425
00:36:39,200 --> 00:36:41,540
It's my knees.

426
00:36:42,220 --> 00:36:43,380
Of course.

427
00:36:48,990 --> 00:36:52,300
When your mother made her walk of atonement,

428
00:36:52,960 --> 00:36:55,470
she did it to get back to you.

429
00:36:55,630 --> 00:36:57,930
I still don't understand why you want to put her

430
00:36:57,930 --> 00:36:59,860
through any more than she's already endured.

431
00:36:59,860 --> 00:37:03,650
It's not what I want. It's what the gods want.

432
00:37:03,700 --> 00:37:06,030
They make their will known to us and it's up to us

433
00:37:06,030 --> 00:37:08,350
to either accept or reject it.

434
00:37:10,860 --> 00:37:12,160
Please.

435
00:37:17,650 --> 00:37:20,860
If we're to be just and good,

436
00:37:20,860 --> 00:37:23,810
then we accept it, all of us, even kings.

437
00:37:23,850 --> 00:37:28,080
A true leader avails himself of the wisest counsel he can.

438
00:37:28,080 --> 00:37:30,440
And no one is wiser than the gods.

439
00:37:33,210 --> 00:37:35,690
My grandfather once said something similar.

440
00:37:36,820 --> 00:37:38,980
Except for the part about the gods.

441
00:37:39,020 --> 00:37:42,220
The gods worked through him whether he knew it or not.

442
00:37:43,510 --> 00:37:45,630
As they work through your mother.

443
00:37:47,700 --> 00:37:49,750
There's so much good in all of us.

444
00:37:50,100 --> 00:37:52,980
The best we can do is to help each other bring it out.

445
00:38:21,630 --> 00:38:22,830
Who are you?

446
00:38:23,580 --> 00:38:24,640
No one.

447
00:38:26,980 --> 00:38:28,960
Who were you before you came here?

448
00:38:29,960 --> 00:38:31,440
Arya Stark.

449
00:38:33,290 --> 00:38:35,700
Tell me about Arya Stark's family.

450
00:38:36,050 --> 00:38:38,040
Her father was Eddard Stark.

451
00:38:38,940 --> 00:38:41,080
Her mother was Catelyn Stark.

452
00:38:41,340 --> 00:38:44,780
She had one sister, Sansa,

453
00:38:45,780 --> 00:38:47,250
and four brothers.

454
00:38:56,430 --> 00:38:57,860
Three brothers.

455
00:38:58,180 --> 00:39:01,170
Robb, Bran, Rickon.

456
00:39:03,230 --> 00:39:06,140
And a half-brother Jon.

457
00:39:07,250 --> 00:39:08,850
And where are they now?

458
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:12,220
They may be dead for all a girl knows.

459
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:24,560
Tell me about the Hound.

460
00:39:26,250 --> 00:39:27,590
Also dead.

461
00:39:38,020 --> 00:39:40,260
Arya Stark left him to die.

462
00:39:40,260 --> 00:39:41,300
He was on her list.

463
00:39:43,910 --> 00:39:45,740
He was not on her list anymore.

464
00:39:47,240 --> 00:39:48,900
She had taken him off it.

465
00:39:49,320 --> 00:39:52,760
Why? Didn't she want him dead any longer?

466
00:39:56,750 --> 00:39:58,790
She did and she did not.

467
00:40:02,960 --> 00:40:04,870
She sounds confused.

468
00:40:10,620 --> 00:40:13,980
Yes, she was.

469
00:40:18,620 --> 00:40:21,630
Who else was on Arya Stark's funny little list?

470
00:40:22,630 --> 00:40:24,130
Cersei Lannister.

471
00:40:25,800 --> 00:40:27,210
Gregor Clegane.

472
00:40:28,830 --> 00:40:30,260
Walder Frey.

473
00:40:34,230 --> 00:40:35,870
That's a short list.

474
00:40:40,670 --> 00:40:43,250
That can't be everyone you want to kill.

475
00:40:46,400 --> 00:40:48,650
Are you sure you're not forgetting someone?

476
00:40:52,100 --> 00:40:54,510
Which name would you like a girl to speak?

477
00:41:30,650 --> 00:41:32,860
If a girl tells me her name,

478
00:41:32,890 --> 00:41:34,620
I will give her eyes back.

479
00:41:38,520 --> 00:41:40,130
A girl has no name.

480
00:41:44,450 --> 00:41:45,490
Come.

481
00:42:18,610 --> 00:42:20,480
If a girl is truly no one,

482
00:42:21,060 --> 00:42:22,520
she has nothing to fear.

483
00:42:48,950 --> 00:42:50,050
Who are you?

484
00:42:54,310 --> 00:42:55,270
No one.

485
00:43:05,740 --> 00:43:08,630
The Umbers are a famously loyal house.

486
00:43:08,740 --> 00:43:11,180
Famously loyal to the Starks.

487
00:43:11,190 --> 00:43:13,940
And you, Lord Karstark.

488
00:43:14,750 --> 00:43:17,180
Your people share blood with the Starks, don't they?

489
00:43:17,480 --> 00:43:19,800
But here we are. Times change.

490
00:43:20,080 --> 00:43:22,430
When my father became Warden of the North,

491
00:43:22,430 --> 00:43:24,570
your house refused to pledge their banners.

492
00:43:24,570 --> 00:43:26,050
Your father was a cunt.

493
00:43:29,820 --> 00:43:31,580
My beloved father, the Warden...

494
00:43:31,580 --> 00:43:35,310
Your father was a cunt and that's why you killed him.

495
00:43:36,330 --> 00:43:38,090
I might have done the same to my father

496
00:43:38,090 --> 00:43:40,560
if he hadn't have done me the favor of dying on his own.

497
00:43:40,630 --> 00:43:43,290
My father was poisoned by our enemies.

498
00:43:45,950 --> 00:43:48,910
Why have you come to Winterfell, Lord Umber?

499
00:43:48,920 --> 00:43:52,080
The bastard Jon Snow led an army of wildlings past the Wall.

500
00:43:53,270 --> 00:43:55,570
We're farther north than any of you fuckers.

501
00:43:55,750 --> 00:43:58,720
Wildlings come down, we always have to fight them first.

502
00:43:58,720 --> 00:44:01,520
I like fighting wildlings. Been doing it all my life.

503
00:44:02,260 --> 00:44:04,650
But there are too many of them for us to beat back alone.

504
00:44:04,790 --> 00:44:07,770
So now you've come seeking help?

505
00:44:08,060 --> 00:44:09,500
We need to help each other.

506
00:44:10,200 --> 00:44:11,200
The colder it gets,

507
00:44:11,200 --> 00:44:13,630
the farther south those goat fuckers will roam.

508
00:44:14,300 --> 00:44:15,730
Won't take them long to get here.

509
00:44:15,730 --> 00:44:18,560
You think a horde of wildlings can take Winterfell?

510
00:44:18,560 --> 00:44:20,630
If they get Jon Snow leading them, maybe.

511
00:44:20,630 --> 00:44:22,740
He knows this place better than we ever will.

512
00:44:26,290 --> 00:44:28,120
Pledge your banners to House Bolton.

513
00:44:28,490 --> 00:44:31,040
Swear loyalty to me as Warden of the North

514
00:44:31,060 --> 00:44:33,550
and we will fight together to destroy the bastard

515
00:44:33,550 --> 00:44:35,310
and all his wildling friends.

516
00:44:35,310 --> 00:44:37,220
I'm not kissing your fucking hand.

517
00:44:37,540 --> 00:44:40,390
Traditionally a bannerman kneels before his lord.

518
00:44:40,390 --> 00:44:41,790
I'm not doing that either.

519
00:44:42,080 --> 00:44:45,290
Why would I trust a man who won't honor tradition?

520
00:44:45,430 --> 00:44:47,490
Your father honored tradition.

521
00:44:49,020 --> 00:44:50,790
Knelt for Robb Stark.

522
00:44:50,790 --> 00:44:52,580
Called him King of the North.

523
00:44:53,110 --> 00:44:55,360
Was Robb Stark right to trust your father?

524
00:44:55,360 --> 00:44:57,430
Then it appears we're at a bit of an impasse.

525
00:44:57,430 --> 00:45:00,130
Fuck kneeling and fuck oaths.

526
00:45:00,760 --> 00:45:02,010
I've got a gift for you.

527
00:45:04,980 --> 00:45:08,090
A girl, I hope. I prefer redheads.

528
00:45:08,090 --> 00:45:10,570
A girl, aye.

529
00:45:12,530 --> 00:45:13,890
A wild one.

530
00:45:22,380 --> 00:45:23,630
I like them wild.

531
00:45:24,830 --> 00:45:28,220
And the boy, nice and young.

532
00:45:28,610 --> 00:45:30,360
The way Karstark likes them.

533
00:45:37,210 --> 00:45:38,160
Who's this?

534
00:45:38,500 --> 00:45:39,850
Rickon Stark.

535
00:45:47,810 --> 00:45:49,840
How do I know that's Rickon Stark?

536
00:46:20,650 --> 00:46:23,190
Welcome home, Lord Stark.

537
00:46:34,950 --> 00:46:36,010
It's time.

538
00:47:14,300 --> 00:47:16,920
If you have any last words, now is the time.

539
00:47:17,590 --> 00:47:18,980
You shouldn't be alive.

540
00:47:19,680 --> 00:47:20,890
It's not right.

541
00:47:22,860 --> 00:47:24,410
Neither was killing me.

542
00:47:28,760 --> 00:47:30,700
My mother's still living at White Harbor.

543
00:47:31,550 --> 00:47:32,690
Could you write her?

544
00:47:33,630 --> 00:47:35,750
Tell her I died fighting the wildlings.

545
00:47:44,520 --> 00:47:47,680
I had a choice, Lord Commander.

546
00:47:48,280 --> 00:47:52,010
Betray you or betray the Night's Watch.

547
00:47:52,420 --> 00:47:55,480
You brought an army of wildlings into our lands.

548
00:47:57,150 --> 00:48:00,130
An army of murderers and raiders.

549
00:48:00,200 --> 00:48:03,360
If I had to do it all over knowing where I'd end up,

550
00:48:04,170 --> 00:48:06,640
I pray I'd make the right choice again.

551
00:48:07,650 --> 00:48:09,390
I'm sure you would, Ser Alliser.

552
00:48:09,400 --> 00:48:12,510
I fought, I lost.

553
00:48:14,920 --> 00:48:16,150
Now I rest.

554
00:48:17,190 --> 00:48:20,370
But you, Lord Snow,

555
00:48:21,280 --> 00:48:23,690
you'll be fighting their battles forever.

556
00:50:11,040 --> 00:50:12,590
We should burn the bodies.

557
00:50:14,680 --> 00:50:15,660
You should.

558
00:50:25,160 --> 00:50:26,630
What do you want me to do with this?

559
00:50:27,350 --> 00:50:28,290
Wear it.

560
00:50:29,030 --> 00:50:29,920
Burn it.

561
00:50:30,970 --> 00:50:32,090
Whatever you want.

562
00:50:33,350 --> 00:50:34,830
You have Castle Black.

563
00:50:41,960 --> 00:50:43,430
My watch is ended.

